    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nWhen an owner is created without a `registrationDate`, the server now defaults it to the current date, and the field is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format. A supplied date is kept as-is.\n\n## Changes\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since `Owner` extends `OwnerFields` via `allOf`, the field flows through the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` (input) and `OwnerDto` (output), and `format: date` generates a `java.time.LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field mapped to a `registration_date DATE` column, with getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps it by name in both directions, so no mapper changes were needed.\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, after mapping the DTO, set `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when it's `null`.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. The tests use the `hsqldb` profile with `schema.sql` initialization; the others were updated for consistency.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `coreDefaultsTotoday` \u2014 no date supplied \u2192 returns today's date \u2705\n- `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` \u2014 `2020-06-15` supplied \u2192 returned unchanged \u2705\n\nFull suite: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
